This product is a derivative work: its Unity format handling is hand-ported
from the projects below. Their copyright notices are kept per the MIT License,
and every ported source file carries a one-line attribution to the file it was
ported from.

AssetStudio -- https://github.com/Razviar/assetstudio (MIT)
  Copyright (c) Perfare, RazTools, Razviar
  Source of truth for AssetBundle, SerializedFile, TypeTree and class layout,
  for the plain texture format conversion (Texture2DConverter.cs, Half.cs),
  for which block or Crunch decoder each texture format goes to
  (Texture2DConverter.cs), for the Xbox 360 byte swap (Texture2DConverter.cs),
  for the vertical flip (Texture2DExtensions.cs), and for sprites: the crop,
  the packing rotation and the tight-mesh mask (SpriteHelper.cs, Mesh.cs).
  The mask's triangle fill reproduces the behaviour of the ImageSharp.Drawing
  version AssetStudio uses (Six Labors, Apache-2.0); it is reimplemented, and
  no ImageSharp code is copied.

UnityPy -- https://github.com/K0lb3/UnityPy (MIT)
  Copyright (c) K0lb3
  Secondary reference and oracle used to generate the test goldens. Source of
  the Switch texture deswizzle (helpers/TextureSwizzler.py,
  export/Texture2DConverter.py), which AssetStudio does not have.

AssetsTools.NET -- https://github.com/nesrak1/AssetsTools.NET (MIT)
  Copyright (c) 2020 nesrak1
  UnityPy's Switch deswizzle is based on its SwitchSwizzle.cs.

texture2ddecoder-wasm -- https://github.com/fatal10110/texture2ddecoder-wasm (MIT)
